    "body": "Independent receiving accepts this exact source for ordinary integration.\n\nHead `de24842a91314fdb89e1b8121d206693fbceb5d3`, tree `cbe35389f27031b0c0162fec7ebfd5e6053d5b0f`, is qualified on actual current main `b9c24ace6b57a17215a53c50b674bd187d13f8ed`. I independently read the production change, frozen behavioral cases, complete current-source tree, actual hosted checkout graph and full maintained/browser logs. [Run 37793910271](https://github.com/Jacob-Met/ledgerly/actions/runs/37793910271) passes 205 Python tests plus 96 subtests, 88 frontend tests, audit/build and the existing CSV controls. [Run 37793910451](https://github.com/Jacob-Met/ledgerly/actions/runs/37793910451/job/113368229714) passes all eight real-browser groups and 14 artifacts with unchanged source.\n\nThe [independent actual-PDF receipt](https://github.com/Jacob-Met/ledgerly/blob/7e8ee4b902e2595680d0651f77e5df90db0356e0/docs/receiving/invoice-record-7879c2abc07f/native-packet/independent-print-font-qualified.json) receives all 79 USD and 75 JPY printed HTML text parts, and directly inspects every page of both original PDFs. Literal Japanese, 海 and emoji, wrapped items, separate ledger/provider values, the exact recorded payment and boundary footer are readable without observed clipping or overlap. Its secondary-reader compatibility normalization is explicit; product strings are unchanged. The old font-limited actual result remains preserved beside the standard CJK-font receiver successor.\n\nI independently verified the [durable packet](https://github.com/Jacob-Met/ledgerly/blob/7e8ee4b902e2595680d0651f77e5df90db0356e0/docs/receiving/invoice-record-7879c2abc07f/native-packet/index.json): all 610 qualified source leaves exact, all 25 previous nonmetadata evidence files unchanged, all 41 indexed files linked to their exact Git blobs, and the sealed independent receipt linked verbatim. The final workflow changes only font setup; all other 24 runtime inputs and all 31 built assets match the prior current-base run.\n\nFresh PR/main reads match the qualified identities, with no review threads or change requests. Acceptance covers the authored sandbox snapshot and recorded browser/font environment. Physical printing, arbitrary platform font coverage, provider effects and restore are outside this scope. Proceeding with the normal expected-head merge; the resulting main-push gates will be received separately."
  },
